# Controls what `git archive` ships — which is what `scripts/new-project.sh`
# uses to bootstrap a derived project (A-05).
#
# The blueprint is both a TEMPLATE and a working repo. Its own lifecycle folders
# therefore hold real, tracked work items — BUG plans, audit registers, review
# records. Without this, a freshly bootstrapped project opens with the
# BLUEPRINT's active bugs sitting in its docs/doing/, which its agents then read
# as their own. Observed: a test bootstrap inherited BLUEPRINT-AUDIT-2026-07-23.md
# and PLAN-BUG-001.md as if they described the new project.
#
# Switching bootstrap to `git archive HEAD` stopped untracked and gitignored
# files (a .env holding SONAR_TOKEN, logs/, node_modules/) from shipping. It does
# NOT stop TRACKED work items — those need an explicit export boundary, which is
# what this file is.
#
# The structure ships; this repo's contents do not. README.md explains each
# lifecycle state and HANDOVER.md is the canonical resume template a new project
# fills in — both are template material and stay.

docs/doing/**                      export-ignore
docs/doing/README.md              -export-ignore
docs/doing/HANDOVER.md            -export-ignore

docs/waiting-acceptance/**         export-ignore
docs/waiting-acceptance/README.md -export-ignore

docs/done/**                       export-ignore
docs/done/README.md               -export-ignore

# backlog/ additionally keeps BACKLOG.md and BUGS.md: unlike the folders above,
# those are empty tables with only a header row — genuine templates a new project
# fills in, not this repo's parked work. If the blueprint ever parks real items
# there, they need listing here too.
docs/backlog/**                    export-ignore
docs/backlog/README.md            -export-ignore
docs/backlog/BACKLOG.md           -export-ignore
docs/backlog/BUGS.md              -export-ignore
